"cell_type":"Astrocytes","gene_id":"ENSG00000088832","module":"turquoise","kme":0.21458,"hub":false,"module_direction":"higher in AD","module_padj":0.500479,"module_significant":false},{"cell_type":"CUX2+","gene_id":"ENSG00000088832","module":"turquoise","kme":0.456468,"hub":false,"module_direction":"higher in AD","module_padj":0.789273,"module_significant":false},{"cell_type":"CUX2-","gene_id":"ENSG00000088832","module":"turquoise","kme":0.344322,"hub":false,"module_direction":"higher in AD","module_padj":0.787198,"module_significant":false},{"cell_type":"Inhibitory","gene_id":"ENSG00000088832","module":"turquoise","kme":0.162638,"hub":false,"module_direction":"higher in AD","module_padj":0.795497,"module_significant":false},{"cell_type":"Microglia","gene_id":"ENSG00000088832","module":"turquoise","kme":0.139513,"hub":false,"module_direction":"higher in AD","module_padj":0.396297,"module_significant":false},{"cell_type":"Oligodendroglia","gene_id":"ENSG00000088832","module":"brown","kme":0.192122,"hub":false,"module_direction":"higher in AD","module_padj":0.137697,"module_significant":false},{"cell_type":"Vascular.niche","gene_id":"ENSG00000088832","module":"blue","kme":0.474479,"hub":false,"module_direction":"higher in AD","module_padj":0.548873,"module_significant":false}],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000088832","entrez_id":["2280"],"uniprot":["P62942"],"ncbi_summary":"The protein encoded by this gene is a member of the immunophilin protein family, which play a role in immunoregulation and basic cellular processes involving protein folding and trafficking. The protein is a cis-trans prolyl isomerase that binds the immunosuppressants FK506 and rapamycin. It interacts with several intracellular signal transduction proteins including type I TGF-beta receptor. It also interacts with multiple intracellular calcium release channels, and coordinates multi-protein complex formation of the tetrameric skeletal muscle ryanodine receptor. In mouse, deletion of this homologous gene causes congenital heart disorder known as noncompaction of left ventricular myocardium. Multiple alternatively spliced variants, encoding the same protein, have been identified. The human genome contains five pseudogenes related to this gene, at least one of which is transcribed. [provided by RefSeq, Sep 2008].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"P62942","text":"Keeps in an inactive conformation TGFBR1, the TGF-beta type I serine/threonine kinase receptor, preventing TGF-beta receptor activation in absence of ligand. Recruits SMAD7 to ACVR1B which prevents the association of SMAD2 and SMAD3 with the activin receptor complex, thereby blocking the activin signal. May modulate the RYR1 calcium channel activity. PPIases accelerate the folding of proteins. It catalyzes the cis-trans isomerization of proline imidic peptide bonds in oligopeptides."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_03","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}